.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-browser-stealth-test 1  "rev-stealth-browser-stealth-test " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-browser\-stealth\-test \- Run a stealth self\-test: launch a stealth browser, navigate to the target detection page (defaults to bot.sannysoft.com), wait briefly, then dump UA / viewport / title
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth browser stealth\-test\fR [\fB\-\-target\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-stealth\fR] [\fB\-\-dwell\fR] [\fB\-\-headed\fR] [\fB\-\-chrome\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a stealth self\-test against a detection page (default: bot.sannysoft.com). Launches the browser with the chosen profile + stealth level, dwells N seconds, then dumps UA / viewport / title for offline inspection. AUTHORIZED TARGETS ONLY.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR [default: https://bot.sannysoft.com/]
Detection page to probe
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR [default: mobile\-ios]

.TP
\fB\-\-stealth\fR \fI<STEALTH>\fR [default: full]

.TP
\fB\-\-dwell\fR \fI<DWELL>\fR [default: 5]

.TP
\fB\-\-headed\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-chrome\fR \fI<CHROME>\fR

.RS
May also be specified with the \fBREV_STEALTH_CHROME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth browser stealth\-test
  $ rev\-stealth browser stealth\-test \-\-profile desktop \-\-dwell 8
  $ rev\-stealth browser stealth\-test \-\-target https://bot.sannysoft.com/ \-\-headed

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Stealth probe completed.
  1  UserError        Unknown \-\-profile / \-\-stealth slug.
  2  TransientError   Chrome launch/CDP transient failure.
  3  PermanentError   Chrome binary missing or unsupported stealth level.

ENV:
  REV_STEALTH_CHROME  Override the chrome executable path (else auto\-detect).
